1,"text":"Evan Rodrigues Goal (4) Snap Shot, assists: Timo Meier (5), Arseny Gritsyuk (7)","type":{"id":"505","text":"Goal","abbreviation":"goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:20"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"11"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3648008","displayName":"Evan Rodrigues","shortName":"E. Rodrigues"},"type":"scorer"},{"athlete":{"id":"3899978","displayName":"Timo Meier","shortName":"T. Meier"},"type":"assister"},{"athlete":{"id":"4915855","displayName":"Arseny Gritsyuk","shortName":"A. Gritsyuk"},"type":"assister"}]},{"id":"401892700000000820","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":1,"text":"Dylan Strome faceoff won against Arseny Gritsyuk","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:20"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"23"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3899933","displayName":"Dylan Strome","shortName":"D. Strome"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4915855","displayName":"Arseny Gritsyuk","shortName":"A. Gritsyuk"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1826","fullName":"Prudential Center","address":{"city":"Newark","state":"NJ","zipCode":"07199","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1826.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":15035,"officials":[{"fullName":"Dylan Blujus","displayName":"Dylan Blujus","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Trevor Hanson","displayName":"Trevor Hanson","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Ryan Jackson","displayName":"Ryan Jackson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Morgan MacPhee","displayName":"Morgan MacPhee","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Kolyachonok scores go-ahead goal, Hellebuyck makes 26 saves as Devils beat Capitals 5-2","description":"— Vladislav Kolyachonok scored the go-ahead goal early in the third period and Connor Hellebuyck made 26 saves as the New Jersey Devils beat the Washington Capitals 5-2 on Thursday night in the first of a two-game set.","story":"NEWARK, N.J. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565274/vladislav-kolyachonok\">Vladislav Kolyachonok</a> scored the go-ahead goal early in the third period and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3020225/connor-hellebuyck\">Connor Hellebuyck</a> made 26 saves as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-capitals\">Washington Capitals</a> 5-2 on Thursday night in the first of a two-game set.\n\n\r\n              Kolyachonok’s shot trickled past Capitals goaltender <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4272888/logan-thompson\">Logan Thompson</a> at 6:27. It was the first game in a Devils uniform for the 25-year-old defenseman, who signed in July as a free agent. He was in the lineup in place of the injured <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587933/johnathan-kovacevic\">Johnathan Kovacevic</a>.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3648008/evan-rodrigues\">Evan Rodrigues</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149245/lenni-hameenaho\">Lenni Hameenaho</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562623/stefan-noesen\">Stefan Noesen</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565222/jack-hughes\">Jack Hughes</a> also scored for the Devils, who have won seven straight home games. Hellebuyck returned to the ice after the Devils held him out of <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/devils-jets-score-2e9c39b3d8ecae8614c497fcb8e290a1\">Tuesday's loss at Winnipeg</a>, the team that traded him to New Jersey last month.\n\n\r\n              Hellebuyck was booed by Jets fans and said <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/connor-hellebuyck-winnipeg-jets-new-jersey-devils-2fd01123d7188a0bdec0745ce9074bd1\">incidents involving his family</a> had prompted his demand to be traded. He has won his first six starts with New Jersey.\n\n\r\n              The Devils are 12-3-0 in their last 15 games and 9-2-0 overall at Prudential Center. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149172/ryan-leonard\">Ryan Leonard</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024833/pierre-luc-dubois\">Pierre-Luc Dubois</a> scored for the Capitals, who had their two-game winning streak stopped. Thompson stopped 24 shots.\n\n\r\n              Rodrigues opened the scoring on the power play 2:20 into the first. Leonard tied it on the power play later in the period.\n\n\r\n              Dubois put the Capitals ahead early in the second. Hameenaho knotted the score 2-2 with his first goal this season, deflecting Brendan Dillon's shot past Thompson.\n\n\r\n              Noesen scored at 17:07 of the third, and Hughes had an empty-netter.\n\n\r\n              The Devils, who missed the playoffs last season, are second in the Metropolitan Division with 28 points.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              The teams play again Saturday in Washington.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-13T03:00:34Z"}}